 "how": "the package's physical statements, each conditional on the lane's supplied parent (its compact E8 action on the punctured elliptic surface, its background, Wilson and spin data) and the analytic hypotheses of its own kernel and domain theorems, which the notes say are not independently checked. As the notes derive them: three end constructions (the relative gauge register, the fixed-fibre puncture, the modular-cusp extension) act on different operator data, so equal integer labels alone supply no map between them; the actual inner action on the physical half-root kernel is one common character, eta_h chi_R(h)^-1, so the fixed odd-spin three-mode block carries a scalar inner action and cannot be identified with the native axis triplet (an equivariant map has rank at most one, and zero for the trivial character); across the three non-trivial spin sectors the three parity characters do occur; an explicit isometry of the full field theory exchanges a spin character with a central core-lift character, identifying sixteen descriptions in four orbits, with a relative character left on the registering action; the coupling at the retained Wilson crossing obeys the normalised relation with the current's charge, strictly above sqrt 2 in the cusp metric; where both charged kernel spaces split as two form modes and one spin mode the leading cubic has rank at most two and the third mass is a second-order duty; the four-slot field maps intertwine the mass operator and transport its complete graph domains. Main verified the finite algebra under each (physical-ij-01) and none of the analysis",
